# GitHub Workflow

## Pushing Changes
- Always use the GitHub CLI (`gh`) and `git` for GitHub operations (reading files, checking commits, pushing, creating PRs)
- After completing any coding task, commit and push changes to GitHub
- Use concise, descriptive commit messages that summarize what changed
- Do this automatically at the end of every task -- don't wait for the user to ask
- If there are no changes to commit, skip silently

## Git Safety
- NEVER use `git push --force` or `git push -f` -- use `--force-with-lease` if needed
- Always `git pull` before pushing if behind the remote
- NEVER run destructive commands (`git reset --hard`, etc.) on shared branches without explicit user confirmation
- NEVER change repo visibility to public or push to a public repository

## Secrets
- NEVER hardcode API keys, secrets, or tokens in source code
- Use environment variables (e.g. `.env.local`, `process.env.*`)
- Before committing, verify no secrets are present in the diff
